[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Englund Gambit"]
[Variation "Englund Gambit: Main Line"]
[ECO "A40"]
[Character "tactical,gambit"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,pin"]
[Themes "accept-the-pawn,block-with-bishop"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "gambit"]
[Opponent "1...e5"]
[Start "orthodox 1.d4"]

1... e5 { The Englund Gambit: Black gives a pawn for quick play and some traps. } 2. dxe5 { Take it. The gambit is not sound, and the tricks only work if White goes wrong. } 2... Nc6 ( 2... d6 3. exd6 Bxd6 ( 3... Qxd6 4. Qxd6 Bxd6 5. Nc3 ) ( 3... cxd6 4. Nc3 ) 4. Nc3 Nc6 ( 4... Nf6 5. Nf3 ) ( 4... Be6 5. Nf3 ) 5. Nf3 ) ( 2... f6 3. exf6 Nxf6 ( 3... Qxf6 4. Nf3 ) 4. Nf3 { White is a clean pawn up. If ...Nc6, it is the same as 2...Nc6 3.Nf3 f6 4.exf6 Nxf6. } ) ( 2... Qe7 3. Nf3 { Develops and guards e5. After ...Nc6 this is the main line. } ) 3. Nf3 { Defends e5 and develops. } 3... Qe7 ( 3... Bc5 4. Nc3 Nge7 ( 4... d6 5. Bf4 ) ( 4... f6 5. Bf4 ) ( 4... Qe7 { Transposes to 2...Bc5 3.Nf3 Qe7 4.Nc3 Nc6. } ) 5. Bf4 { Guards e5 a second time with the bishop outside the pawn chain. } ) ( 3... Nge7 4. Nc3 Ng6 5. Bg5 { Develops and hits the queen on d8, on a square the knight on g6 cannot reach. } ) ( 3... d6 4. exd6 Bxd6 5. Nc3 { Transposes to 2...d6 3.exd6 Bxd6 4.Nc3 Nc6 5.Nf3. } ) ( 3... f6 4. exf6 Nxf6 5. e3 ) 4. Bf4 { Defends e5 a second time with the bishop that is already outside the pawn chain. } 4... Qb4+ ( 4... d6 5. exd6 cxd6 6. Nc3 ) 5. Bd2 { The right block. Other blocks lose a piece (see the traps) because the queen on b4 also hits the bishop on f4. } 5... Qxb2 ( 5... Qe7 6. Nc3 ) 6. Nc3 { Brings the knight out and clears the first rank. If the queen takes the rook on a1, the white queen takes it back. } 6... Bb4 ( 6... Nb4 7. Nd4 { The knight covers c2, so ...Nxc2+ is impossible, and Ndb5 or Rb1 next hunts the queen. Rb1 at once would lose to ...Nxc2+. } 7... Na6 8. e3 ) 7. Rb1 { Attacks the queen, which has to leave b2 with the rook on a1 now safe. } 7... Qa3 ( 7... Qxc3 $2 8. Bxc3 Bxc3+ 9. Nd2 { Black has only a bishop and a pawn for the queen. } ) 8. Rb3 { Attacks the queen again with tempo and keeps her away from the b-file. } 8... Qa5 9. e4 { Takes the centre now that White is a pawn ahead and nearly fully developed. } 9... Nge7 ( 9... Bxc3 10. Bxc3 { White keeps the extra pawn and gets the bishop pair. } ) 10. a3 { Asks the bishop on b4 what it wants to do. After ...Bxc3 Bxc3 the bishop pair and the extra pawn are safe. Plan: Bd3, castle, and keep the extra pawn. } *
